# Binary files must never have their line endings rewritten.
#
# core.autocrlf is true in this repo, so git converts LF to CRLF on checkout for
# anything it considers text. Git guesses by looking for NUL bytes near the
# start of a file, and that guess FAILS for ReportLab PDFs: they are ASCII85
# encoded, so there are no NULs to find. partnerships.pdf was classified as text
# and a fresh checkout inflated it from 5,199 to 5,304 bytes -- 105 line feeds
# rewritten as CRLF -- which corrupts the file.
#
# PNG and JPG are detected correctly on their own; they are listed anyway so the
# rule is about the category rather than the one file that happened to break.
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.m4a  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
